\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. When on my day of life 
\par the night is falling,
\par And in the winds, from unsunned
\par spaces blown,
\par I hear far voices out of darkness calling,
\par My feet to paths unknown,
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Be near me when all else is from
\par me drifting-
\par Earth, sky, home's pictures, days
\par of shade and shine,
\par And kindly faces, to my own uplifting
\par The love which answers mine.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. I have Thee, my Father; let 
\par Thy Spirit,
\par Be with me then to comfort and uphold;
\par No gate of pearl, no branch of palm 
\par I merit,
\par Nor street of shining gold.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Suffice it if- my good and ill unreckoned,
\par And both forgiven through Thy abounding
\par grace-
\par I find myself by hands familiar beckoned
\par Unto my fitting place.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. There, from the music round about
\par me stealing,
\par I fain would learn the new and 
\par holy song,
\par And find at last, beneath Thy 
\par trees of healing,
\par The life for which I long.
\par                        Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

